On the day of the market in 2017, the public market price was increased by HK$59.7**, with the first day in excess of HK$110 billion**, and was branded by the media as the "Insurance Technology Unicorn" "The Future of China's Financial Technology." The ants group, the Quemours, and the three safe-singers were created -- three names that were the reason investors were willing to give 10 times P/B.

In May 2026, the CPS ** 12.2 Hong Kong Dollar**, market value ** HK$ 20.6 billion**. In the same period, the premium income rose from $5.954 billion to **35.735 billion - a sixfold increase**. Income increased sixfold, and the market value fell by 80%.

This is not simply an overestimation or an underestimation to explain. It shows a fundamental change in the market’s pricing logic for this company**: from a technology company to a financial company (P/B about **0.77 **, which is cheaper than China’s peace of mind).

** The same company, dressed differently, had a price difference of 10 times.** The first thing to understand is to figure out which one it should wear.

